{"name":"Floral Bluff","hex":"#e7cfb9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"floral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or connected with flowers.","Portraying flowers, especially in a stylized way."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A design involving flowers","A perfume redolent of flowers"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floral"},{"term":"bluff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of bluffing; a false expression of the strength of one’s position in order to intimidate or deceive; braggadocio.","An attempt to represent oneself as holding a stronger hand than one actually does."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a bluff; to give the impression that one’s hand is stronger than it is.","To frighten, deter, or deceive with a false show of strength or confidence; to give a false impression of strength or temerity in order to intimidate or gain some advantage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bluff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.